#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## 01 Tool synthesis: repeated action sequences found in the journal
## become tools; model calls fall, and what transfers.
##
## Run with "just run-exp 01". A deterministic simulation on the
## Workshop world: the model is Workshop's expert (always right), so
## what differs between groups is only how many times it is called and
## what each call costs. Assumed costs (tokens): a model call 500; the
## model writing a tool or a hint 1500 each, once; each tool's schema
## adds 20 to every prompt, each hint's text 60. A model given hints
## ignores them on every 4th call. Groups:
##   A        fixed harness: one call per op
##   B        memory: the learned sequences as hints in the prompt
##            (in-context, as XSkill and agentrail-rs do)
##   C        tools: the same sequences as tools the harness runs
##   C-short  tools of at most 3 ops

"po:" u_se< "Policy"
"jr:" u_se< "Journal"
"ws:" u_se< "Workshop"

### Training: the fixed harness's own history

## Eight tasks of devices made from 1 wood and 1 ore.
train := 8 3 r_eshape 1 1 1 3 1 1 2 1 1 5 1 1 1 1 1 4 1 1 2 1 1 3 1 1
(dt, jt) := (train, po:n_one 8, 0, 500) po:w_orkload 200
"training (group A): tasks done, model calls, tokens"
dt
po:c_alls jt
jr:t_otal jt

### What is learned from it

## The three sequences of 2 to 8 ops worth the most calls, and the
## three of 2 or 3 ops.
tools := (2, 8, 3, 8) po:s_ynthesize jt
short := (2, 3, 3, 8) po:s_ynthesize jt
"learned (one row per tool, op codes, 0 padding):"
tools
"learned, at most 3 ops:"
short
"the first tool by name:"
first := 1 s_elect tools
'ws:n_ame m_ap (w_here first != 0) s_elect first
learn := 1500 * t_ally tools

### Held out

## Same recipe, other sizes; then shifted recipes (2 wood, 2 ore).
same := 4 3 r_eshape 2 1 1 4 1 1 6 1 1 3 1 1
shift := 4 3 r_eshape 2 2 1 3 1 2 2 2 2 4 1 3
## Tasks done, calls and tokens of a harness on a task set.
u:r_esult := { (tasks, T, extra, every) ->
  (d, j) := (tasks, T, 1, 500, extra, every) po:w_orkloadWith 200
  d c_at (po:c_alls j) c_at jr:t_otal j
}
u:g_roups := { tasks ->
  a := u:r_esult (tasks, po:n_one 8, 0, 0)
  b := u:r_esult (tasks, tools, 60 * t_ally tools, 4)
  c := u:r_esult (tasks, tools, 20 * t_ally tools, 0)
  cs := u:r_esult (tasks, short, 20 * t_ally short, 0)
  4 3 r_eshape a c_at b c_at c c_at cs
}
"held out, same recipe; rows A, B, C, C-short; columns tasks done, calls, tokens:"
s1 := u:g_roups same
s1
"held out, shifted recipes; rows A, B, C, C-short:"
s2 := u:g_roups shift
s2

### Paid back?

## Tokens on both held-out sets together (A, B, C, C-short); then the
## tokens each learning group saved against A, less what learning cost
## (1500 a tool or hint, three each; group A learns nothing).
tok := (3 s_elect_2 s1) + 3 s_elect_2 s2
"tokens on all 8 held-out tasks, A, B, C, C-short:"
tok
"net tokens saved against A after paying to learn, B, C, C-short:"
((f_irst tok) - 1 d_rop tok) - learn
